    "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
    "direct judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
    "direct judge left implication lean_implies_source unclear"
  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "The disagreement concerns selection scope, not the meaning of the Lean proposition. The exact locator selects the sound-speed definition, equation (1.7), and its classification sentence. For that selection, the derivation is inherited explanatory context rather than an additional conclusion that this classification theorem must establish. The round-trip judgment's weaker classification applies to the broader conjunction extracted by the source contract.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 3 separately states that (1.7) can be obtained from (1.5), then classifies (1.7) as hyperbolic. The locator specifically anchors the sentence classifying the equation. The elaborated target asserts only IsHyperbolic(wavePrincipalPart(sqrt(K/rho)))."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "Resolve the selection in favor of the locator's classification claim. The coefficient encoding is sufficient for that claim; it is not sufficient for a combined derivation-and-classification claim. Interpret the material parameters within the source's ordinary acoustic setting.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 2 identifies K and rho as material bulk modulus and density and c as sound speed. Printed page 3 distinguishes derivation from classification. D001 and D002 encode the classification of the displayed equation."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The blind translation accurately recovers the target. Its absence of pressure, velocity, and derivatives establishes that no derivation is represented, but this is not an omission from the specifically located classification assertion. Consequently the round-trip failures C02, C05, C07, N01, and N06 do not apply to the selected classification claim.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind dossier has only two real parameter binders and a coefficient predicate. The source classifies the equation itself, independently of a particular solution or the derivation used to obtain it."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Resolve to faithful-equivalent for the classification assertion in its inherited physical acoustic context. This does not certify equivalence to the broader conjunction in the extracted source contract.",
      "primary_evidence": "Equation (1.7) has normalized coefficients (1, 0, -c^2), with c = sqrt(K/rho) from printed page 2. D001, D002, and D028 test positivity of precisely the corresponding discriminant."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "The positive material-parameter premises make the ordinary physical acoustic domain explicit. They are an interpretation of inherited context, not verbatim inequalities from these pages. Regularity assumptions are unnecessary for classifying the principal coefficients.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 2 describes waves in a gas or elastic solid, identifies rho as density and K as bulk modulus, discusses rightward sound propagation with c > 0, and identifies sqrt(K/rho) as sound speed. The target explicitly requires K > 0 and rho > 0."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "The selected classification conclusion is complete. The contract's additional derivation conclusion is a correct extraction of nearby source content but broadens the selected assertion. A theorem for that broader assertion would need the acoustic-system-to-wave-equation implication, which this target does not contain.",
      "primary_evidence": "The locator names the classification sentence after (1.7). The source places the derivation in a separate preceding sentence. The target preserves the defining sound-speed expression and all three principal coefficients."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "Relative to ordinary positive-density, positive-bulk-modulus acoustics, the target exposes the inherited parameter domain rather than establishing a stronger theorem. It is a specialization relative to an unrestricted algebraic family with arbitrary real material coefficients, but the selected pages do not assert the classification for that unrestricted family.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 2 introduces K and rho as physical material constants. The explicit target quantifies over real scalars subject to two strict positivity premises; it does not quantify over arbitrary sound speeds independently of those constants."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "The target correctly excludes zero density and zero sound speed in the selected acoustic setting. It neither relies on totalized division by zero nor on the negative-input branch of Real.sqrt. No classification of degenerate or nonphysical parameters is certified.",
      "primary_evidence": "D016 defines the nonnegative real square root through NNReal. Positive K and rho ensure K/rho > 0. At K = 0 and rho = 1, D001, D002, and D028 instead give discriminant zero, illustrating why an unrestricted reading would be invalid."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "N06 is not applicable to the selected classification assertion: it asserts neither solution existence nor uniqueness nor a regularity-dependent differential implication. The source's differentiation argument has analytical requirements, but these belong to the separate derivation statement.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 3 first describes differentiation and elimination, then separately classifies the equation. The target and D001–D007 concern only real principal coefficients."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve the positivity assumptions as an explicit rendering of the inherited physical material setting. Their absence as printed inequalities should be documented, but it does not warrant treating the source as a claim about every real pair K and rho.",
      "primary_evidence": "The attached printed page 2 identifies the quantities as density, bulk modulus, and sound speed in ordinary acoustic media. The blind translation correctly reports both strict positivity premises."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The coefficient representation is an equivalent abstraction for classification, because that property depends on the principal coefficients rather than a chosen solution. It is not an equivalent representation of the separate differential derivation. Positivity supplies the intended physical domain and is not genuine theorem strengthening.",
      "primary_evidence": "The classification sentence refers to equation (1.7). The direct local declaration specifies the principal expression timeTime * p_tt + timeSpace * p_tx + spaceSpace * p_xx, and D002 supplies (1, 0, -c^2)."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "No boundary mismatch occurs within the interpreted physical domain. The theorem makes no assertion about zero or negative material parameters. Extending the source's classification to such parameters would require a separate source interpretation and cannot be inferred from this acceptance.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target's explicit premises exclude those parameter values. D028 evaluates the discriminant to 4*(sqrt(K/rho))^2, which is strictly positive on the admitted domain."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication lean_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "The implication holds for the located classification claim in the inherited acoustic domain: substitute the source's sound speed, identify the normalized principal coefficients, and interpret positive discriminant as second-order hyperbolicity. It does not establish the neighboring derivation.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed pages 2–3 provide c = sqrt(K/rho) and p_tt = c^2 p_xx. D001 and D028 impose b^2 - 4*a*d > 0, and D002 supplies a = 1, b = 0, d = -c^2."
    },
    {
      "item": "Independent dependency and reuse review",
      "resolution": "All supplied dependencies have consistent task-specific effects. D001–D007 construct and inspect the three principal coefficients. D008, D009, D013, and D018 implement real division in the source's quotient order. D010 and D014 supply strict real comparison. D011, D015, D017, D023, and D026 supply the intended numerals. D012 supplies real scalars. D016 supplies the nonnegative square root, with positive input here. D019–D021, D024, D029, and D030 supply ordinary natural powers, specifically squaring. D022 and D025 supply the negative spatial coefficient. D027 and D028 supply real discriminant arithmetic. The reused declarations introduce no altered domain, numeral, operation, or interpretation in this target.",
      "primary_evidence": "The complete inline inventory supplies the declaration types and bodies, including the entries abbreviated by reuse records in the review packet. Their expansion gives 0 < 0^2 - 4*1*(-(sqrt(K/rho))^2), equal to 0 < 4*K/rho under the target premises."
    },
    {
      "item": "Discriminant convention, nonvacuity, and strength",
      "resolution": "The full mixed-derivative coefficient convention agrees with b^2 - 4*a*d. The alternative convention using twice the mixed coefficient has the same sign here because the mixed coefficient vanishes. The domain is nonempty: K = rho = 1 gives discriminant 4. Acceptance therefore rests on a substantive nondegenerate classification, with no claim of stronger applicability.",
      "primary_evidence": "The supplied local structure documentation identifies the full mixed coefficient; D002 sets it to zero; D028 defines the discriminant. The explicit premises admit K = rho = 1."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "For the locator's classification assertion in the inherited physical acoustic context, the principal coefficients of (1.7) are (1, 0, -c^2), where c = sqrt(K/rho). The Lean conclusion states that their discriminant is positive, exactly expressing second-order hyperbolicity for this equation. Positive physical material parameters give the target's premises. This implication is not an assertion that discriminant positivity entails the separate acoustic-system derivation."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Apply the source's classification to positive bulk modulus and density, substitute its definition c = sqrt(K/rho), and normalize (1.7) to p_tt - c^2*p_xx = 0. Under the supplied full mixed-coefficient convention, its hyperbolicity is 0 < 0^2 - 4*1*(-c^2), precisely D001 applied to D002. The discriminant is 4*K/rho > 0."
    }
  },
  "classification": "faithful-equivalent",
  "accepted": true,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The selected pages do not explicitly axiomatize the admissible material parameters. Acceptance uses their ordinary physical acoustic interpretation; it does not establish agreement with an unrestricted or generalized-material parameter domain.",
    "The supplied source contract includes the neighboring derivation as an additional conclusion, whereas the locator specifically anchors the classification assertion. This decision follows the locator. If the benchmark instead requires the combined derivation-and-classification result, this target is not-faithful-weaker and must not inherit this acceptance."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "source-contract-scope",
      "evidence": "The locator specifically selects the sound-speed definition, equation (1.7), and its classification sentence. The contract also records the separate preceding derivation as a required conclusion. The target contains no functions or acoustic-system implication.",
      "impact": "The target is accepted for the located classification assertion only. It cannot certify coverage of the broader conjunction extracted in the contract."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "implicit-physical-domain",
      "evidence": "The source names physical density, bulk modulus, and sound speed without printing K > 0 and rho > 0 as explicit hypotheses. The target states these inequalities.",
      "impact": "These premises are accepted as making inherited physical context precise, not as verbatim source hypotheses or as theorem strengthening."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Independent inspection of the attached primary-source images and the complete inline declaration evidence establishes an exact coefficient and sound-speed match for the specifically located second-order classification assertion. The source separates this assertion from the preceding derivation; the contract's broader extraction explains the judges' disagreement but does not make that derivation part of the locator's classification claim. On the ordinary physical acoustic domain, both implication directions hold, the discriminant convention is consistent, and the hypotheses are nonvacuous. All dependency effects were reassessed from the supplied evidence rather than inferred from reuse provenance. No tools, target proof, external source, or prior audit files were consulted, and no source or rendering hashes were independently recomputed."
}
